This repository is orchestration/glue only: it does not vendor, bundle, or
modify the source code of the tools it integrates (PostHog, n8n, LiteLLM,
Twenty, Slack). Those tools are pulled as their own official images/services
and are governed by their own licenses:

  - PostHog  — MIT (core); `ee/` directory proprietary
  - n8n      — Sustainable Use License (fair-code, source-available)
  - LiteLLM  — MIT (core); `enterprise/` directory proprietary
  - Twenty   — AGPL-3.0 (with an "Application Exception" for API use)
  - Slack    — proprietary service

Running these as separate services and calling them over their published
network APIs does not place this repository under their licenses. See
docs/COMPLIANCE.md and README.md for details. This is not legal advice.
